From 3bfdb8b6e24cd446c45260ef8d3df9915d029cfa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nusage <dev@nusage>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 13:52:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Add Nushell support

A profile for Nushell scripts and modules (*.nu) and NUON data (*.nuon), with
the tree-sitter-nu grammar.

Nushell predeclares the `def`s and `extern`s of a block before parsing its
pipelines, so their order in a script, a module or any other block does not
matter and they commute, keyed by name. `use` statements commute among
themselves. Everything else in a block runs in order (pipelines, `let`,
`const`, `alias`) and is left alone. Record entries commute, keyed by their
key; the spread of another record is kept in place. The commands a `use`
imports, `use foo [a b c]`, commute too.

Lists, tables, pipelines, match arms and command parameters keep their order:
a concurrent insertion at the same place in one of them stays a conflict.

Strings, interpolated strings and the shebang are merged as a whole.

The grammar's separators between entries (commas, whitespace) are hidden
tokens, so the newline separator is used when elements are added on both
sides; a formatter puts an inline record back on one line.
